00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:20.500
Seven kings throughout the Middle Kingdom
were contending for supremacy.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.450
After 500 long years of upset,

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:29.410
the people had nearly given up
all hope of peaceful times ahead.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:36.360
Chin

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:36.360
Gi

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:36.360
Kan

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:36.360
Sho

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:36.360
So

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:36.360
Se

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.540
But in the year 246 BCE, in the land of Chin

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.830
along the western border of the Middle Kingdom,

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.790
Destiny's favored King took the throne.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:47.790
This man was the future emperor of Chin:
the 31st King of Chin, Ei Sei.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:52.620
At the same time, there lived a man
who shone with a fierce brightness.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.540
He supported Ei Sei
with an uncommon strength

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.000
and strove to be the greatest
general on earth: Shin.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.100
"Hi"

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.700
This is the tale of two men
working toward one lofty goal:

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.700
a unified Middle Kingdom.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.910
Let's go!

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.790
We are the Hi Shin Force!

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.870
Kinjo Castle, Six Months Earlier

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.330
The Encroaching Coalition Army

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:52.660
It's been a month. Zero action.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:56.200
It's not so bad. We could all use a break.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.660
Well, yeah, but...

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.410
Get 'em, Den Ei!

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.330
I got money on you, Den Yuu-- shape up!

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:07.450
Now that the Hi Shin Force
has a thousand men, we're fearless!

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:11.910
True enough. Chin's on a roll,
having taken Sanyou from Gi

