00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.810
Tougun

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:16.370
and made their army post
into Tougun.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.120
Other countries won't be
bothering us for a while.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.250
You got that right!

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.580
Are you worried about Ri Boku?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.120
I can give you this warning here and now:

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:38.830
You may be racking up
combat experience, but in fact,

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:43.620
you do not understand the true terror of war.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.330
The true terror?

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.700
Shin!

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.700
Enemy forces have appeared
in the eastern mountains!

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.750
The Hi Shin Force is needed as reinforcements!

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.790
Let's go, Hi Shin Force!

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.250
What are <i>you</i> doing here, Mou Ten?
You're with the Gaku Ka Force!

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.870
Aw, come on. My body's getting rusty, too.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.790
What?!

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.000
So it's not an enemy army--
it's one of ours?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.040
How does such a stupid mix-up even happen?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.750
Er, well, we're not the usual friendly
forces found in these parts...

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.640
Roku O Mi! And Commander Kan Ou!

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.970
Roku O Mi

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.970
Kan Ou

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.220
Roku O Mi and Kan Ou?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.500
Formerly of General Ou Ki's troops...

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.580
What could the Tou Army be doing out here?

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.000
Are you two stationed here at Kinjo too?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:45.040
Don't be ridiculous.
We were investigating Sho, So, and Gi.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.500
"Investigating"?

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.620
The Tou Army, too...

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:57.830
Ou Ki had his own independent information network.
Tou has now taken that over.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.750
An information network?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:07.080
Tou says a storm is brewing--
one greater than Bayou, where we lost Ou Ki.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.660
Greater than Bayou...

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:27.570
Fort Nanko, Some Days Later

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:28.040
In the south of Chin, along its border
with their massive neighbor So,

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.660
Chin had built a long and winding
wall of defense: Fort Nanko.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:36.080
It was the very manifestation
of Chin's terror of the So army.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.620
This is one dull mission, all right.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.080
If they try anything here, it's instant war.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.950
No one could attack even if they wanted to--
not even the So army.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:52.250
Or so everyone thought. However...

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:55.350
Chin Army General - Tou

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.290
So they've come at last.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.890
"So"

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.330
It can't be!

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:10.040
It's So! So is attacking!

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.030
Kanyou, Kingdom of Chin

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.580
Wh-What is this?!

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.780
Chin Minister of the
 Left - Shou Bun Kun

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.160
Are you absolutely certain?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.040
Yes, sir. They've already breached Fort Nanko.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.160
Our defensive forces were wiped out.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.330
They've breached our protective wall?!

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.500
So, that huge country...

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.750
They've made a move against Chin?

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.050
So Army General -
 Rin Bu Kun

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.200
Let's go.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.370
Make immediate preparations
for a council of war!

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.080
How many men in So's army?

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:46.870
Fifty thousand--
but more armies are on their way.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.540
The details are unclear!

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:51.580
So doesn't have 50,000 men, surely!

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.620
And which castle is So attacking now?

00:07:54.620 --> 00:08:00.000
The enemy is marching ever northward,
paying no mind to any castles along the way.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.910
They have come as far as Yasen!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.200
Yasen?!

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.120
Yasen is in the middle of southern Chin!

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.160
They've made it all that way?

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.290
This is bad.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:13.290
Why would the enemy ignore
castles and simply advance?

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.390
Never mind that! Right now we--

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.910
Stop panicking, you fools!

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:21.160
Ch-Chancellor, sir!

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.180
Chin Chancellor - Ryo Fui

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.750
Ryo Fui...

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:28.290
We had observed some
suspicious activity of late.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:34.700
Hence we stationed two great generals,
Chou Tou and Mou Bu, to defend the south.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:42.620
Chin Minister of the 
Right - Shou Hei Kun

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.000
Isn't that right, Shou Hei Kun?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.410
Yes.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:42.580
However, it seems the foe has formulated
countermeasures against these two generals.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.790
They purposely breached
the difficult-to-attack Fort Nanko

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:58.680
Chin

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:58.680
So

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:53.040
to reach the interior in one fell swoop,
without battling Chou Tou and Mou Bu.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.700
Once the first 50,000-man unit reaches
the other side of our defensive line,

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.950
the main forces will likely invade.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:03.290
But once we have 50,000
enemy troops inside that defensive line,

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:11.610
Chin

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:11.610
Gi

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:11.610
Kan

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:11.610
So

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:07.290
they will act like a strong
poison invading the body:

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:12.160
As the poison runs wild in
the southern region, it will rot and die.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:15.950
So Chin may well lose its southerly lands...

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.250
Surely both generals have already
left their castles and mobilized!

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:23.040
No one knows better the danger
inherent in a breach of our defensive line

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.160
than the generals there on the scene!

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.830
And yet...

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:33.790
We cannot know from here
if they will make it in time.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.880
Chin Army General
 Mou Bu

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.770
Chin Army General
 Chou Tou

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.750
Quickly! We'll take the So army!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.330
Check.

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:56.160
Scout report! If we keep going,
the So army will break through first!

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.360
So Army - First Unit

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.040
Keep moving forward!

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:07.960
So Army Battalion 
Commander - Kou Yoku

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:01.660
Chin's got a sad excuse for an army, all right!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.750
We can slip right past them
without even crossing swords!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.540
Don't want us to come up from behind, now!

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.540
Eh?

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.540
Huh?

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.830
Who the hell is <i>that</i> ?

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.200
The Chin army!

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.700
The enemy's arrived! Three--no, 5,000 of them!

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.000
Ha! 5,000? To stop <i>50</i> ?

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:26.870
Dou Kin. Rin Bou.
This southern defense is in dire straits.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:30.120
The faster we move, the greater the benefit.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:31.120
Sir!

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:32.870
Let's go!

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:39.790
Mou Bu, sir!

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.910
An urgent report from our scout!

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:47.040
Tou's 5,000-man army has engaged
So troops on the Fandou Plain!

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.700
Wh-What?!

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:54.580
They have stopped the enemy--
now our troops will surely reach the blockade first!

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.000
Tou's army... Ou Ki's former troops?

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.410
Still, 5,000 against 50,000...

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.700
"So" "Tou"

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:16.250
What gives? These guys aren't half bad!

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:24.530
So Army Battalion 
Commander - Haku Rei

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:22.540
Be sure you aim for their vital spots!

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.450
We'll never take them down otherwise!

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.410
Sir!

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:29.750
Arrow wounds don't slow them down.
These must be their finest troops.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:37.120
One of their generals?

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:38.910
Stand down, Rei.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.120
Dou Kin?

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:51.700
This fellow...

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:52.910
...is capable.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:56.830
I am Dou Kin, commander of the fifth Tou Army!

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:03.080
C-Commander Dou Kin...

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.200
Dou Kin...

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.370
Meanwhile,

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:15.370
as word of So's invasion reached
Shin and his troops on the eastern front,

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:21.800
Chin

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:21.800
Tougun

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:21.800
Kan

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:21.800
So

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:21.800
Gi

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:18.250
orders were issued to join the battle against So,

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:22.660
leaving a small defensive contingent
at Tougun.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:29.450
And while the Hi Shin Force was
the first to leave for the battlegrounds...

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:31.250
That's the Gi army!

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:33.620
Th-There must be a hundred thousand of 'em!

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:36.500
And they're headed for Chin!

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:39.750
Don't tell me So's not
the only one on the attack!

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:40.910
Dammit!

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:41.910
Shin!

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:44.450
We can't do anything against <i>that</i> !

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.790
I sure ain't gonna keep it to myself!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.210
Castle in the Anti-Gi Defensive Zone
Saki Castle

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.120
That was quick.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:08.250
We have no use for such a trifling castle.
Let's join up with the main forces.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.750
And the prisoners?

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:14.410
We must show Sanyou's rage to the world.

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:20.540
I lost family in Sanyou.
I'll carry that grudge till the day I die.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.120
Get rid of them all.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.660
We didn't make it...

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.000
There was nothing we could do.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:38.040
With the way they split up
and worked to stay undiscovered,

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.660
we were bound to be too late.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:43.870
"Nothing we could do"?

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:46.080
Hundreds were killed here!

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:51.910
But why is the enemy nowhere to be found?

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:55.540
They finally capture a castle,
then just leave it behind?

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.540
They're after a bigger one.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.290
I'm borrowin' this.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:04.870
Goryou Castle, the anti-Gi
defensive base, <i>is</i> up ahead.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.290
Sorry we were late!

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:13.250
We don't have time to bury you all right now!

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:18.330
We gotta move fast so there
won't be even one more victim!

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:19.660
Please understand!

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:23.620
And in return, we <i>will</i> avenge you!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:29.250
First, we defend Goryou Castle
so we can keep damage to a minimum!

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.120
I'm bettin' the Gi army's
main forces'll be there, too!

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:34.080
Let's go, Hi Shin Force!

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:49.950
Goryou Castle... has fallen! But how?

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:55.000
What the hell is HQ doing?!
Didn't they send in reinforcements from behind?

00:14:55.000 --> 00:15:00.540
They took our anti-Gi
defensive base like it was nothing!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.000
How do you fight all-out invaders like <i>that</i> ?

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.870
W-We <i>can't</i> -- not on our own...

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:11.000
But we can't count on the troops inside, either.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:15.500
HQ will have sent the troops
on our side of the line south

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.000
to handle the So invasion.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:20.000
No... So that's all...

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.790
All we can do is follow 'em.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:26.750
I ain't sure what that'll accomplish,
but I can't just leave 'em be.

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:29.410
Chin's gonna be in a heap of trouble.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.830
Kanyou, Kingdom of Chin

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.080
News of the Gi invasion reached Kanyou as well.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.370
So and Gi are working in tandem.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.080
There can be no doubt.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:49.660
But we never received word that
the two nations were even in contact!

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:52.330
We hadn't heard as much either,

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:56.200
but there were reports that Ri Boku
may have been in touch with So.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.700
Then Ri Boku is behind the scenes,
pulling the strings?

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:08.000
I wouldn't put it past him.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:10.790
Ri Boku...

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:14.620
If he is, then the Sho army
is on its way as well!

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:16.580
Th-That can't be!

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.540
Urgent report! The Sho army has breached
our borders! They're invading!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.500
Bayou is surrounded and under attack!

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:27.160
Oh, no! This is terrible!

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:30.500
Surely the three countries
must have an alliance!

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:34.000
A map! Bring us a bigger map!

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.000
An allied army of three nations?!

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:40.040
Our hands were full enough with So alone!

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.540
Shou Bun Kun!

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:45.830
Reconsider the positions and manpower
of all the armies in Chin's command!

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.290
Re-establish our defensive front
with the utmost haste!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.330
Sir!

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:51.160
Ki! Your fastest horse!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:54.580
Send support to every southbound
army defending against So!

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:55.370
Sir!

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:58.250
This is three countries at once.
Can we stop them?

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:02.290
We must--with all the troops at our command!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:05.330
You realize that Shou Hei Kun
is our military's high commander.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.700
Of course I do!

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:11.830
Kou Ryuu! Gather all intelligence
from every quarter.

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:12.660
Sir!

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:17.370
Son Kou! Issue a state of emergency
to all domestic castles

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:19.790
and instruct them to take up
a Rojo footing.

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:20.290
Sir!

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:23.790
Kai Yoku. Prepare our troops
in the interior to move out!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.910
Mobilize them once we have
a firm line of defense.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:26.540
Sir!

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.250
Urgent report!

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:31.410
Enough! What is it <i>this</i> time?

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:35.410
A-An urgent report from the northeast!

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:40.080
En army of 120,000 has taken Sui,
our base along the northeastern front,

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:42.870
and is poised to invade our country!

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:51.040
-- <i>What</i> ?!
--Urgent report!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.540
Kan army of 50,000 has invaded at Shoku!

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.950
There are signs that Se to our east,

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:00.410
is also establishing a large army
and moving through Sho to Chin!

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:05.410
The armies of six nations?
Have they joined forces?

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.540
What in blazes?

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:12.540
<i>What in blazes</i> ?!

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:17.870
A coalition army!

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:20.700
A... a coalition army?

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.830
Yes--without a doubt.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:30.250
An allied army of multiple countries
joined together against a single foe.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.500
Th-That's ridiculous!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:38.830
Even during these long years of strife,
no coalition army has ever--

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:42.540
No: there was one time
it evolved into full-on war.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:49.730
Chin

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:49.730
Kan

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:49.730
Gi

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:49.730
Sho

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:49.730
So

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:49.730
Se

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:49.730
En

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:46.410
It was about 40 years ago.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:50.160
Six nations took up arms against
the then-massive eastern country of Se.

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:56.200
They were led by commanding
general Gaku Ki of En,

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:58.700
"Chin" "Kan" "Gi" "So" "Sho" "En"

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.080
which had taken the brunt of the damage.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:05.080
Royal Capital 
Linzi

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:05.290
Se lost all of its territory,
apart from its castles at Sokuboku and Kyo.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:13.540
Then we, too, could suffer
the misfortune of losing our country.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:20.950
Ten! The Gi army is further to the right!

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:23.250
We can get the jump on them this way!

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.450
Commander! To the left!

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.200
The Kan army!

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:30.580
They're invading Chin, too?

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.370
No way!

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:34.540
Now hang on a second...

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:37.120
What the <i>hell</i> is happening?!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.320
The So Army

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.570
The Gi Army

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.820
The En Army

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.080
The Kan Army

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.330
The Se Army

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:51.580
The Sho Army

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:01.290
Report! The castle at Bayou has fallen!

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:04.950
General Kei Sha has brought
all within under his control!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:10.730
Sho Chancellor and General 
Ri Boku, one of the Three Greats

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:09.160
Understood. In that case...

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.790
All armies, advance!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:14.120
Ri Boku, sir.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:16.160
You're not smiling.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:22.910
Only because, as the one who
plotted this coalition army,

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:25.870
I know what's about to happen.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:33.750
Incidentally, the troops are baffled to be
passing up the castles along the way.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:38.910
Right now we're invading as quickly
as we can to paralyze the heart of Chin.

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:40.080
Paralyze it?

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:45.700
If they're attacked by six countries
at once with speedy invasions,

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:50.700
Chin's headquarters will be thrown
into utter confusion, unable to think.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.910
When that happens...

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:57.690
Kanyou, Kingdom of Chin

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:56.160
...it will be over in a flash.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:00.020
Sho

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.540
The Sho army has passed Hou hills!

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:03.080
The En army is now in Etsu!

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:04.330
The Kan army is currently--

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:05.780
Kan

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.950
A situation like this...

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.660
Where on earth does one even begin?

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:19.080
Remain calm. One error in our handling
now and there'll be no going back.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.370
Urgent report!

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:22.450
The Gi army has passed Chuuken!

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:25.750
Chuuken? They've come so far already?

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.080
This is bad.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.200
Stand up.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.500
Your Highness!

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.040
Have you knotholes for eyes?

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:41.040
Are your heads mere decoration?

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:43.080
Look at this map.

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:46.200
At this moment, in every corner of this country,

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:50.700
tens of millions are about to lose their lives!

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.910
The only ones who know
the entirety of this situation

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:54.910
are here in this chamber!

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.700
We are also the only ones
who can work against it!

00:21:57.700 --> 00:21:59.500
Do you understand?

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:05.580
The 30-odd people here now hold
the lives of all of Chin's people in their hands!

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:08.160
Do not be distracted by some mighty foe!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:10.540
At every moment, our country is--

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:13.250
our <i>people</i> are being violated!

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:17.750
Devote every fiber of your being to finding
a countermeasure, a way out of all this!

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:20.750
Coalition army or no,
they cannot do as they will!

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:22.120
We will fight!

00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:31.910
Even that lot...

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:34.120
...in Ryo Fui's faction...

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:36.540
Hurry! We must evacuate all the people we can!

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:40.120
Get them as far as possible
out of the coalition army's path!

00:22:41.660 --> 00:22:44.540
While it's good to see we've
regained our fighting spirit,

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:49.450
spirit alone won't turn the tides
of battle, Shou Hei Kun.

00:22:49.450 --> 00:22:50.660
No.

00:22:50.660 --> 00:22:56.120
We do have one means by which to drive
a wedge into the coalition army's advance.

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:57.410
A wedge?

00:22:57.410 --> 00:22:59.910
Our target is the great nation to the east:

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:02.110
Se

00:22:59.910 --> 00:23:01.120
Se.

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:07.620
The Hi Shin Force rode onward,
unaware of the situation.

00:23:07.620 --> 00:23:13.200
Shin alone had an inkling
about the man behind it all.

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:16.790
Ri Boku...

00:24:52.510 --> 00:25:02.020
A Coming Together.

00:24:54.290 --> 00:24:58.120
Next time on <i>Kingdom</i> : "A Coming Together."
